{"id":65,"date":"2015-09-18T11:33:00","date_gmt":"2015-09-18T18:33:00","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/gamescrye.wpengine.com\/?p=65"},"modified":"2017-09-24T18:32:31","modified_gmt":"2017-09-25T01:32:31","slug":"overcoming-game-design-limitations","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/gamescrye.com\/blog\/overcoming-game-design-limitations\/","title":{"rendered":"Overcoming Game Design Limitations"},"content":{"rendered":"<p>Game design constraints is a topic that deserves some analysis. This is one of those seemingly hidden forces that greatly impacts every aspect of a game. As a designer, whether you realize it or not, you are constantly guided by limiting factors. Keeping an eye out for these hurdles can make it easier to focus on a creative solution, and turn around what could otherwise negatively impact the game.<\/p>\n<p>Here\u2019s a great video produced by the guys at <a href=\"https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/channel\/UCGPMrF9AN_D9BrmSmMeV3hA\">Game Soup<\/a> that showcases examples of video game design limitations and some solutions to these problems.<\/p>\n<p><iframe title=\"Ingenious Solutions in Video Game Design: A Long-form Analysis\" width=\"500\" height=\"281\" src=\"https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/embed\/2Xa7qM1o18c?feature=oembed\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allowfullscreen><\/iframe><\/p>\n<h2>Know Your Limits: Recognizing Design Constraints<\/h2>\n<blockquote><p>\u201cWhen forced to work within a strict framework the imagination is taxed to its utmost \u2013 and will produce its richest ideas. Given total freedom the work is likely to sprawl.&#8221;<\/p>\n<p>\u2014 T.S. Eliot<\/p><\/blockquote>\n<p>Not all games start out with a limitless array of options. In fact, no game does. They all have some predefined requirements and decisions already made that guide the entire design. These are inherent design constraints that come to the surface throughout the development process.<\/p>\n<p>Constraints on game design can include things such as:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>The platform the game is being developed for<\/strong>. This can affect screen sizes, computing power, input devices, etc. By knowing the platform and their limitations ahead of time,\u00a0you can pick an appropriate game engine, plan assets and design the interface better.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Technical bugs or limitations<\/strong>. Whether it&#8217;s memory limitations on a mobile device, or framerates on a browser, games will always push the boundaries of computers further than any other medium. If you find yourself in this camp, try obfuscating the issue with clever design or by looking at modifying\u00a0a game rule in a way that can free up resources and trick the gamer\u00a0into seeing what you intended in the first place.<\/li>\n<li><strong>A game with pre-existing Intellectual Property (IP)<\/strong>. It can restrict choices on the story, artwork, or even game mechanics depending on the specific property. In a situation like this it might be best to double down on what is unique about that IP, instead of just adding more of the same.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Limited resources<\/strong>. Such as with limited budgets, small teams, no skills in certain disciplines, or running up against a hard deadline. If you need an artist, go on one of the many <a href=\"https:\/\/www.unrealengine.com\/marketplace\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">asset stores<\/a> to save time and money. Don&#8217;t have time to finish your design? Find some procedural algorithms to speed up content development, or remove some mechanics that aren&#8217;t adding a major benefit.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Genre definitions<\/strong>. An FPS isn\u2019t an FPS without shooting people in the first person. Right there you already have defined a camera angle, and some basic game mechanics. Not much can be done here if the game relies on a particular genre for it&#8217;s definition, except to realize\u00a0that within each genre there is a lot of competition and you&#8217;ll want to build something that is unique to your game.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Everyone\u2019s internal design biases<\/strong>. It&#8217;s easy to make assumptions about certain mechanics based on our previous experiences. By pushing\u00a0the design limits, you are breaking free of the cookie-cutter mechanics we are accustomed to seeing. This is the only way\u00a0entirely new niches or even genres can be created.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>Want some great examples from\u00a0games you&#8217;ve likely already played? There\u2019s a Reddit thread with more examples of how various\u00a0<a href=\"http:\/\/www.reddit.com\/r\/Games\/comments\/2r5e1g\/creative_solutions_for_game_design_barriers_whats\/\">game developers solved their design barriers<\/a>.<\/p>\n<p>Now, let\u2019s flip the idea of constraints a bit, and look at a scenario where you can take the idea of limitations and put it in your arsenal of design strategies.<\/p>\n<h2>Constraints on the gamer<\/h2>\n<p>Removing choices to improve a game\u2019s design might sound counter-intuitive, but if done right it can greatly benefit the gamer. Here\u2019s a few examples.<\/p>\n<h3>Decision funnels<\/h3>\n<h4>Example: Guide the gamer down the story<\/h4>\n<p>Some games have a very strong story narrative. Without guiding the gamer down specific paths, forcing them to make decision A or B, the story can get lost in the background. In those situations where you want the gamer to go down a particle path it will be imperative to limit some of the available options they\u2019d normally have.<\/p>\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/gamescrye.com\/\/wp-content\/uploads\/2015\/09\/image03.png\"><img data-srcset=\"https:\/\/gamescrye.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2015\/09\/image03.png 635w, https:\/\/gamescrye.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2015\/09\/image03-300x169.png 300w\" decoding=\"async\" data-src=\"https:\/\/gamescrye.com\/\/wp-content\/uploads\/2015\/09\/image03.png\" class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-84 lazyload\" src=\"data:image\/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAAAAAP\/\/\/yH5BAEAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAIBRAA7\" alt=\"Final Sephiroth battle in Final Fantasy 7\"    sizes=\"(max-width: 635px) 100vw, 635px\" \/><noscript><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-84\" src=\"https:\/\/gamescrye.com\/\/wp-content\/uploads\/2015\/09\/image03.png\" alt=\"Final Sephiroth battle in Final Fantasy 7\" width=\"635\" height=\"357\" srcset=\"https:\/\/gamescrye.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2015\/09\/image03.png 635w, https:\/\/gamescrye.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2015\/09\/image03-300x169.png 300w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 635px) 100vw, 635px\" \/><\/noscript><\/a><\/p>\n<p>In Final Fantasy 7 the <a href=\"http:\/\/finalfantasy.wikia.com\/wiki\/Sephiroth_%28Final_Fantasy_VII_Boss%29\">final battle with Sephiroth<\/a> is rigged so that you can\u2019t lose the battle. This is an extreme example, where the battle is primarily cinematic. But it inevitably creates the desired effect of furthering the climatic end to the main story.<\/p>\n<p>A perhaps better example of a decision funnel is one where you allow several choices within a very confined space, such as the <a href=\"http:\/\/dragonage.wikia.com\/wiki\/Epilogue_(Origins)\">various missions you must complete in Dragon Age Origins<\/a> that ultimately guide the main game plot. When the gamer is confronted with choices they must make throughout the game, it helps keep the gamer engaged in the story. Especially when they see how their choices have changed the world around them.<\/p>\n<p>Without these decision funnels, you could end up with an open ended world with far less emphasis on a moving story. You may have played one or two of these games where you never felt compelled to perform an action and often lost interest, or ended up lost and unsure what to do next. There may have been lots to do, but not enough guidance toward some overarching goal.<\/p>\n<h3>Remove distractions<\/h3>\n<h4>Example: Help the gamer find clues<\/h4>\n<p>Puzzles in games can be difficult. I remember getting stuck on some of the puzzles in <a href=\"https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Space_Quest_V\">Space Quest V<\/a>, a classic puzzle adventure game. I\u2019d spend hours randomly clicking or trying to figure out how some random item would be used in a scene.<\/p>\n<p>A gamer (like me) might miss the puzzle clues the designer built, if they didn&#8217;t also remove some of the typical level distractions.<\/p>\n<p>Looking at <a href=\"http:\/\/zelda.com\/link-between-worlds\/\">The Legend of Zelda: A Link Between Worlds<\/a>, throughout there are some well thought out puzzles and some subtle clues that help you unravel hidden areas.<\/p>\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/gamescrye.com\/\/wp-content\/uploads\/2015\/09\/image01.png\"><img data-srcset=\"https:\/\/gamescrye.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2015\/09\/image01.png 710w, https:\/\/gamescrye.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2015\/09\/image01-300x177.png 300w\" decoding=\"async\" data-src=\"https:\/\/gamescrye.com\/\/wp-content\/uploads\/2015\/09\/image01.png\" class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-82 lazyload\" src=\"data:image\/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAAAAAP\/\/\/yH5BAEAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAIBRAA7\" alt=\"The Legend of Zelda: A Link Between Worlds, puzzle hint strategy\"    sizes=\"(max-width: 710px) 100vw, 710px\" \/><noscript><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-82\" src=\"https:\/\/gamescrye.com\/\/wp-content\/uploads\/2015\/09\/image01.png\" alt=\"The Legend of Zelda: A Link Between Worlds, puzzle hint strategy\" width=\"710\" height=\"418\" srcset=\"https:\/\/gamescrye.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2015\/09\/image01.png 710w, https:\/\/gamescrye.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2015\/09\/image01-300x177.png 300w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 710px) 100vw, 710px\" \/><\/noscript><\/a><\/p>\n<p>In one section of the Tower of Hera, while you work your way around paths outside the tower you come to a dead end. With no distractions, it\u2019s easier to notice a platform below you that curiously wraps around the corner. If you follow the hint, and meld into the wall and walk around the corner above the platform you\u2019d be rewarded by advancing to a new location.<\/p>\n<h3>Simplified gameplay<\/h3>\n<h4>Example: Strip away unnecessary game mechanics<\/h4>\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/gamescrye.com\/\/wp-content\/uploads\/2015\/09\/image00.png\"><img data-srcset=\"https:\/\/gamescrye.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2015\/09\/image00.png 806w, https:\/\/gamescrye.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2015\/09\/image00-300x135.png 300w\" decoding=\"async\" data-src=\"https:\/\/gamescrye.com\/\/wp-content\/uploads\/2015\/09\/image00.png\" class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-81 lazyload\" src=\"data:image\/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAAAAAP\/\/\/yH5BAEAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAIBRAA7\" alt=\"Super Meat Boy simplified mechanics are good\"    sizes=\"(max-width: 806px) 100vw, 806px\" \/><noscript><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-81\" src=\"https:\/\/gamescrye.com\/\/wp-content\/uploads\/2015\/09\/image00.png\" alt=\"Super Meat Boy simplified mechanics are good\" width=\"806\" height=\"364\" srcset=\"https:\/\/gamescrye.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2015\/09\/image00.png 806w, https:\/\/gamescrye.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2015\/09\/image00-300x135.png 300w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 806px) 100vw, 806px\" \/><\/noscript><\/a><\/p>\n<p>Something can be said for simplicity. Sometimes removing features and content can enhance gameplay. Case in point: <a href=\"http:\/\/supermeatboy.com\/\">Super Meat Boy<\/a>. No grappling hook upgrades, no armor, no skill levels, just the meat of the game (pun intended) &#8211; a meat-jumping-boy.<\/p>\n<p>There&#8217;s a couple benefits here. It gives the designer an opportunity to focus on a core mechanic, putting a polish on it that would otherwise be difficult to have. Super Meat Boy is said to have very responsive feedback and controls.<\/p>\n<p>It also lowers the learning curve to a new gamer, and shortens the series of feedback loops a player is constantly going through. Trimming the fat can be an important decision, especially for casual games where the attention spans are so short.<\/p>\n<h3>Limit favorable options<\/h3>\n<h4>Example: Ramp up difficulty by removing previously available options<\/h4>\n<p>In situations where a player has a lot of favorable options, such as a wide arsenal of weapons to choose from, or even something simple as a floor to run on, removing some of these resources can present unique challenges. By doing this you force the user to adapt to a new situation, fallback on different tactics and think on their feet.<\/p>\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/gamescrye.com\/\/wp-content\/uploads\/2015\/09\/image02.png\"><img data-srcset=\"https:\/\/gamescrye.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2015\/09\/image02.png 637w, https:\/\/gamescrye.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2015\/09\/image02-300x180.png 300w\" decoding=\"async\" data-src=\"https:\/\/gamescrye.com\/\/wp-content\/uploads\/2015\/09\/image02.png\" class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-83 lazyload\" src=\"data:image\/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAAAAAP\/\/\/yH5BAEAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAIBRAA7\" alt=\"Metroid 2 Return of Samus, challenges designed into metroid battles\"    sizes=\"(max-width: 637px) 100vw, 637px\" \/><noscript><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-83\" src=\"https:\/\/gamescrye.com\/\/wp-content\/uploads\/2015\/09\/image02.png\" alt=\"Metroid 2 Return of Samus, challenges designed into metroid battles\" width=\"637\" height=\"382\" srcset=\"https:\/\/gamescrye.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2015\/09\/image02.png 637w, https:\/\/gamescrye.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2015\/09\/image02-300x180.png 300w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 637px) 100vw, 637px\" \/><\/noscript><\/a><\/p>\n<p>In <a href=\"http:\/\/metroid.wikia.com\/wiki\/Metroid_II:_Return_of_Samus\">Metroid 2: Return of Samus<\/a>, you have 7 weapons you are able to pick up through the progression of the game. In spite of this, virtually all of the metroids are only susceptible to one weapon, your missile weapon was the only effective way to damage them. There are a lot of secondary weapons to choose from for the other enemies, but anytime you face a metroid you are limited to a single option and to make it worse, you have a limited supply of missiles.<\/p>\n<h2>Conclusion<\/h2>\n<p>The important thing to take away here is: no matter the hurdles you may face, it\u2019s always important in finding a solution that can mitigate any negative effects to the gamer. Sometimes the limitations can be used to your benefit.<\/p>\n<p>What other examples of constraints have you seen? Leave a comment below and let us know.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Game design constraints is a topic that deserves some analysis. This is one of those seemingly hidden forces that greatly impacts every aspect of a game. As a designer, whether you realize it or not, you are constantly guided by limiting factors. Keeping an eye out for these hurdles can make it easier to focus [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":67,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"closed","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"content-type":"","_genesis_hide_title":false,"_genesis_hide_breadcrumbs":false,"_genesis_hide_singular_image":false,"_genesis_hide_footer_widgets":false,"_genesis_custom_body_class":"","_genesis_custom_post_class":"","_genesis_layout":"","footnotes":""},"categories":[21],"tags":[],"coauthors":[4],"class_list":["post-65","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","has-post-thumbnail","category-gameplay-resources","entry"],"yoast_head":"<!-- This site is optimized with the Yoast SEO plugin v28.5 - https:\/\/yoast.com\/product\/yoast-seo-wordpress\/ -->\n<title>Overcoming Game Design Limitations - Gamescrye Blog<\/title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Game design 